      <PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>HOUSE OF UKRAINE IS A LONG-STANDING NON-PROFIT ORGANIZATION SINCE 1965. OUR PURPOSE IS TO PROMOTE AND CULTIVATE THE ART, HISTORY, CUSTOMS, LANGUAGE, AND TRADITIONS OF UKRAINE. WE FOSTER AND CULTIVATE A SPIRIT OF UNDERSTANDING, GOODWILL, AND COOPERATION AMONG THE VARIOUS NATIONAL GROUPS REPRESENTED IN THE HOUSE OF PACIFIC RELATIONS, INTERNATIONAL COTTAGES, INCORPORATED (HPR), AND TO BRING UKRAINIAN CULTURE TO THE ATTENTION OF THOUSANDS OF CALIFORNIA RESIDENTS AND TOURISTS EVERY YEAR.HOUSE OF UKRAINE IS RUN BY VOLUNTEERS. OUR ANNUAL PROGRAMS, MOSTLY FREE TO THE PUBLIC INCLUDE 1) OPEN EXHIBITS EVERY WEEKEND AND SOME WEEKDAYS (AVERAGE 15/HRS PER WEEK) TO PARK VISITORS, 2) FREE CULTURAL PROGRAMS OF TRADITIONAL DANCE, MUSIC, SONG ON OPEN STAGE AT HPR, 3) PARTICIPATE IN INTERNATIONAL ETHNIC FOOD SALES UNDER HPR, 4) FOLKART CLASSES AND SPECIAL EXHIBITS THROUGHOUT THE YEAR, MOSTLY FREE BUT SOME WITH NOMINAL CHARGES, 5) OPEN MUSEUM FOR SCHOOL CHILDREN VISITS, LECTURES AND PARTICIPATE IN OTHER IN</PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>ONGOING PROGRAMS RUN BY VOLUNTEERS INCLUDES OPEN MUSEUM THAT RUNS ON EVERY WEEKEND AND SOME WEEKDAYS TO PARK VISITORS;FREE CULTURAL PROGRAMS OF TRADITIONAL DANCE; MUSIC AND SONGS ON OPEN STAGE AT HPR; PARTICIPATE IN INTERNATIONAL ETHNIC FOOD SALES; FOLK ART CLASSES AND SPECIAL EXHIBITS THROUGHOUT THE YEARS. CULTURAL EVENTS,FOLKART CLASSES AND SPECIAL EXHIBIT AND PARTICIPATION IN OTHER INTERNATIONAL CULTURE FAIRS AND EVENTS.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>25303</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
